  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "FAMILY_MEMBER"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "The booking says \"tummy aches, sister has coeliac disease.\" Hi Ellis, I'm Dr Park. Mum, you're on the line too. Who wants to go first? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Me, if that's okay. Ellis's older sister was diagnosed with coeliac disease in March, and since then I can't stop noticing how often Ellis complains about her stomach."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's not that often. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's find out. Ellis, how long have the stomach aches been around?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Since the summer holidays. About three months."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Longer than that. It was Easter, I remember because she missed the egg hunt. That's eight months."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "So somewhere between three and eight months. We don't need to settle it. What are they like?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Like a crampy feeling, around my belly button, after lunch mostly."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anything else going on with your tummy?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I get bloated. My jeans feel tight even when I haven't eaten much."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "And she's tired, she's always asleep on the sofa by seven."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'm not always asleep. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What about your poos?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Loose, sometimes. Pale. Gross."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Have you lost any weight that you know of?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "No, if anything she's grown out of her shoes, so no."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What do you eat on a normal day?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Toast for breakfast, a pasta pot or a sandwich at lunch, and whatever mum cooks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Lots of bread and pasta, yes. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Right. Do you do any sport, Ellis?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Hockey, twice a week. I'm a defender."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And who's at home?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Me, my husband, Ellis and her sister."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anything else in her medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Eczema when she was small."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any operations?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Her adenoids out when she was four. And her appendix, two years ago."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In the family, who else has coeliac disease or autoimmune things?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Her sister, obviously. And my mother has type 1 diabetes."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any allergies?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Possibly. After an antibiotic when she was about two she came out in a rash. I honestly don't know which one."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I don't remember."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll note a possible allergy, unconfirmed. Now, here's what I think. With a sister diagnosed, loose pale stools, bloating and tiredness, this could well be coeliac disease."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "So she should stop eating gluten? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Please don't, yet. If she stops, the blood test can come back falsely normal. Keep eating bread and pasta normally until the tests are done."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Good to know, I'd have started tomorrow. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to arrange a coeliac antibody blood test, a total IgA level, a full blood count, and a ferritin level."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Do I need to fast? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No, eat normally. And I'd like to start ferrous sulfate, 200 mg, once a day, and vitamin D, 1000 units, once a day, in the meantime."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Will the iron upset her tummy? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It can. Take it with food. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  }
 ],
